  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.7.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: afar\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/a/afar/afar-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: edc4fbe9b8a5f55187dd0eb6c4c756561949473cb2b8459c0e4ea8b21d778c42\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - setuptools >=77\n    - setuptools-git-versioning\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - distributed >=2026.1.1\n    - innerscope >=0.8.0\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - afar\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n  # afar reads the caller's source and frames, which change with every Python, so run the\n  # suite (a local Dask cluster) on both the oldest and the newest Python.\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - pytest >=9.0.3\n        - ipython >=8.10\n    script:\n      - pytest -v --pyargs afar\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - python\n        - pytest >=9.0.3\n        - ipython >=8.10\n    script:\n      - pytest -v --pyargs afar\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/eriknw/afar\n  repository: https://github.com/eriknw/afar\n  summary: Run code on a Dask cluster via a context manager or IPython magic\n  description: |\n    afar allows you to run code on a remote Dask cluster using context managers and IPython magics.\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - eriknw\n",
